- [x] need a reload button where it scans the file folders for changes. Should we be polling on a regular basis? I don't want to add background processes if that isn't a good idea, but if it's not out of the norm and won't cause any issues I am down. Give me your best thoughts on it @done(2026-08-31 16:33)
  Shipped both: `r` refreshes manually, and the tree auto-refreshes every ~2s.
  No background process was added — the app already wakes every 250ms when
  idle (that's how autosave and open-file reload work), so the tree refresh
  rides that same tick. It only re-walks *expanded* directories, so it's
  cheap. This is the norm for TUIs. The fancier route is the `notify` crate
  (macOS FSEvents) for instant updates — it does add a watcher thread and a
  dependency; worth it only if 2s ever feels slow.


